From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:30:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] YouTube: featured picture beside its title, Latest videos
 as a grid under it

Concept C from the November 6 featured-video review. From 1024px the featured
picture is capped at 720px (60% of the width at narrow desktops) with its
kicker, title and meta beside it; Latest videos becomes a two-, then (from
1440px) three-across grid under it. From 1920px the five picks sit at the foot
of the title column; from 2560px By channel and Watch later run down the right
of both. Tablets and phones are unchanged.

youtube.js swaps a shown featured picture from hqdefault (480x360) to
maxresdefault (1280x720), else sddefault (640x480), once the larger one loads
at full size; YouTube answers a missing size with a 120x90 placeholder. Without
JavaScript the page keeps hqdefault. The sidebar check now asserts the one- and
two-column grid, the 720px cap and the picture-beside-title layout.

